{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_21\">Problem 21</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 21\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the area of the region bounded by the curves <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/426ff4d2d29a6e4605952c80ee97f30a29541e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y= x^{3} - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09dd395f794711d3fdc2fdf19ee3daafdb46e89c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y= x^{2} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/87266fe273dae9c53610f7e74b5e6f1a496c996a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{5}{4} \\text{ square units} \\quad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{3}{4} \\text{ square units} \\quad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{5}{3} \\text{ square units} \\quad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 1 \\text{ square units} \\quad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{4}{3} \\text{ square units}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"770\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To obtain the bounds, we equate the two functions:\n\\begin{align*}\n\tx^{3} - x &amp;= x^{2} - 1\\\\\n\tx(x^{2} - 1) - (x^{2} - 1) &amp;= 0\\\\\n\t(x-1)^{2}(x+1) &amp;= 0\n\\end{align*}\nThus, the bounds are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16b48ce95294d373707e27381c893d254a360e5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{3} - x &gt; x^{2} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/a/b2a43ac9b944d91adc9d38614ac75f1c4195d743.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in (-1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" />, the area between the curves is\n\\begin{align*}\n\t\\int_{-1}^{1} \\left[ \\left(x^{3} - x\\right) - \\left(x^{2} - 1\\right) \\right]\\, dx\\ &amp;= \\int_{-1}^{1} \\left[ x^{3} -x^{2} - x  + 1 \\right]\\, dx\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\left[ \\frac{1}{4}x^{4} - \\frac{1}{3}x^{3} - \\frac{1}{2}x^{2} + x \\right]_{-1}^{1}\\\\\n\t&amp;=\\frac{1}{4}(1)^{4} - \\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3} - \\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2} + (1) \\\\\n\t&amp; \\qquad \\qquad -\\left( \\frac{1}{4}(-1)^{4} - \\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3} - \\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{2} + (-1) \\right)\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{1}{2} + 1 - \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{2} - 1\\\\\n\t&amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{4}{3} \\text{ square units }}.\n\\end{align*}\n~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High Scho